## Genie Remix — .gitignore
##
## Scoped to what this repository actually is: a C#/VB.NET WinForms desktop app built with the
## .NET SDK on Windows. Trimmed from the generic VisualStudio.gitignore, which carried ~270
## lines for BizTalk, Azure, Silverlight, Paket, Python, SQL Server and other things this
## project has never used.
##
## If you add tooling that needs new ignores, add them here with a comment saying why.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Dd]ebug/
[Rr]elease/
x64/
x86/

# Self-contained publish output (this is what the release ZIP is made from)
publish/
artifacts/
# Release workflow scratch: staging/ is the publish tree, the rest are its outputs
staging/
release-notes.md
SHA256SUMS.txt
Genie-Remix-*.zip

# Symbols and intermediate build files.
# Note: Release builds are configured with <DebugType>None</DebugType>, so PDBs are not
# normally produced. If symbols get shipped as a release asset (see docs/RELEASE-READINESS.md
# M2), they are built in CI and uploaded there — never committed.
*.pdb
*.ilk
*.tmp
*.tmp_proj
*_wpftmp.csproj
*.binlog
*.rsp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime data created beside the executable (portable mode)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CreateGenieFolders() in Forms/FormMain.cs builds these on first launch. They hold the user's
# own settings, scripts, maps and logs. They must never be committed — shipping them would
# overwrite players' data on upgrade, and Logs/ can contain game session content.
#
# Anchored with a leading slash so they only match at the repository root. In particular this
# must not catch Plugin/ (the VB plugin ABI project) or Resources/ (tracked skin bitmaps).
/Config/
/Icons/
/Logs/
/Maps/
/Plugins/
/Scripts/
/Sounds/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local scratch space
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# /scratch/ is a working area for throwaway things that support development but are not part
# of the product: one-off probe programs, diagnostic scripts, captured output, comparison
# dumps, notes in progress. Nothing in it is ever committed.
#
# README.md is the one tracked file, so the folder exists in a fresh clone and explains
# itself rather than appearing as a mystery empty directory.
#
# If something in here turns out to be worth keeping, move it to its real home (docs/,
# .github/, a tools folder) and commit it there. Don't `git add -f` out of scratch — that
# defeats the point of the boundary.
/scratch/*
!/scratch/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — never commit these
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Plugin/GenieStrongKey2020.pfx is the assembly signing key. It is referenced by
# Genie4.csproj (<ManifestKeyFile>) but is deliberately absent from the repository.
*.pfx
*.snk
*.publishsettings
*.pubxml
*.azurePubxml

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# IDE and editor
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vs/
.idea/
*.suo
*.user
*.rsuser
*.userosscache
*.userprefs
*.sln.docstates
_ReSharper*/
*.DotSettings.user
*.[Cc]ache
!?*.[Cc]ache/

# Claude Code — local machine settings, not shared
.claude/settings.json
.claude/settings.local.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OS cruft
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
~$*
*~
*.swp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Misc
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.log
*.vspscc
*.vssscc
Generated\ Files/
MigrationBackup/
_UpgradeReport_Files/
UpgradeLog*.XML
UpgradeLog*.htm

# README embeds two screenshots, and those specific files are tracked. The folder is ignored so
# that ad-hoc local screenshots don't get committed by accident. To add a new one deliberately:
#   git add -f screenshots/your-new-shot.png
screenshots/
.env
